  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA (config_001) achieved 48.5% accuracy, far outperforming image-only ResNet50 (config_010) at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We have no data on whether multiprofile representation (with aggregation) improves upon the single-profile RNA baseline. This experiment (config_002) makes the minimal change from config_001—switching to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation while keeping the same PCA n2000 encoder—thereby isolating the effect of profile setting and aggregation on the strongest modality. It is the best next step because it tests a structural axis (single vs. multi-profile) that, if beneficial, would unlock a large family of downstream configurations (better encoders, multimodal fusion) in the remaining 7 experiments, while if neutral or harmful, it rules out an entire design direction early in the budget."
}

